AudioJudge protocol assets
==========================

This directory contains prompt templates and spoken-label WAV assets copied
verbatim from AudioJudge at commit fc4a1f93fbe10a7e7fd8ea7298269d6e421a57ab:

  https://github.com/Woodygan/AudioJudge

AudioJudge is Copyright (c) 2025 Woody Gan and distributed under the MIT
License reproduced in LICENSE. The original prompt files are
system_prompts.py and system_prompts_pointwise.py. The original spoken-label
files are in signal_audios/.

protocol.py is an Ayase-owned interoperability implementation. It preserves
the released prompt, message-order, concatenation, gap, and caller-labelled
in-context-learning contracts while intentionally replacing the original
temporary-directory and implicit paid-TTS behavior. It requires bundled
signals, uses task-scoped temporary paths supplied by the caller, decodes WAV
input to mono signed PCM16 for heterogeneous-input portability, and never
performs TTS, ASR, or asset downloads. The released source's historical
OpenAI preview default is not retained: the Ayase module declares its current
hosted-model migration separately and makes no numerical-reproduction claim.
